  "id": "23d2f75b-eaef-5278-9845-9cdb9ef16d0f",
  "slug": "berries-and-cream-bars-recipe-8691436",
  "name": "Berries-and-Cream Bars",
  "recipe_type": "dessert",
  "brief_description": "This summer-y snacking cake includes a fluffy white cake, marshmallow creme, berry jam, and freeze-dried fruit.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C) and position rack in center. Lightly grease bottom of a 9-inch square cake pan. Line bottom with parchment paper. Grease and lightly flour parchment and sides of pan."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Whisk flour, baking powder, and salt together in a medium bowl."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Mix butter and oil in the bowl of a stand mixer fitted with a paddle attachment at medium speed until well combined, about 1 minute. Mix in sugar at medium-high speed until light and fluffy, 4 to 5 minutes. Mix in egg whites in 2 or 3 additions at medium speed until well combined, scraping bowl well after each addition. Mix in 1 teaspoon vanilla and the almond extract."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Mix in about 1/3 of flour mixture at low speed. Mix in 1/3 cup milk; scrape bowl well. Repeat, alternating flour mixture and milk, until fully incorporated and batter is smooth."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Spread batter in an even layer in prepared pan. Bake until a toothpick inserted into center comes out clean or with a few moist crumbs, about 30 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Let cool in pan 10 minutes, then run an offset spatula or a knife around edge of cake and invert onto a wire rack. Remove parchment and let cool completely."
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "text": "Using a large serrated knife, halve cake horizontally to make two layers. Transfer one layer, cut side up, to a platter. Top with 1/2 cup jam, spreading evenly. Top with second cake layer, cut-side down."
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "text": "Meanwhile, make berry cream: puree 2/3 cup jam in a blender or mini food processor until very smooth."
    },
    {
      "position": 9,
      "text": "Beat cream in the bowl of a stand mixer fitted with a whisk attachment at medium speed until it begins to thicken, about 1 minute. Mix in marshmallow creme at medium-high speed until soft peaks form. Mix in pur\u00e9ed jam and 1 teaspoon vanilla at low speed until well combined. (If needed, fold whipped cream by hand to more evenly incorporate jam.) Frost top and sides of cake with berry cream."
    },
    {
      "position": 10,
      "text": "For garnish, crush freeze-dried berries with a mortar and pestle (or your hands) into a mixture of small pieces and powder; sprinkle over cake. Cut cake into 12 pieces. Chill in an airtight container until ready to serve, up to 2 days."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 12,
